<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khaqani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1120–c. 1199</span> · Also known as Khaqani Shirvani</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Khaqani was a Persian poet from Shirvan, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a>, and one of the masters of the Persian ode. He served as court poet to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shirvanshah">Shirvanshahs</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuchihr-iii">Manuchihr III</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akhsitan-i">Akhsitan I</a>, was imprisoned for a time, and wrote verses from prison as well as a famous ode on the ruins of the Sasanian palace at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ctesiphon">Ctesiphon</a>. He died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khaqani.jpg" alt="Khaqani" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Elmju · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khaqani_Park3.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
